Notes
  - The 22 required i18n keys already exist (verbatim, web-matching values) in apps/windows/Strings/en/Resources.resw
    (translation.search.*); the page resolves each through the ShellLocalizer → Localization.Get → Resources.resw
    bridge using the web key names. No catalog change was required for this page.
  - The seven web <GlassPanel> JSX occurrences map 1:1 onto the seven native panels (search/filter, the five
    mutually-exclusive state surfaces, the repeated result-group panel) — see the === PARITY === binding evidence.
  - Web <AINLSearch /> (rendered above the search panel) is a SEPARATE shared-component parity unit that returns null
    on the default install (ai_mode 'off' / nl-search feature toggle off); it is not one of this page's 32 parity
    items (the manifest scopes this page to the 7 GlassPanels) and is out of scope here.
  - Search is a request/response source, not a live SSE stream, so ADR-013's ">2 min staleness" indicator is N/A; the
    additive TsDataFreshness chip surfaces last-search freshness / in-flight / error state for header consistency.
  - SI units (P1/S5): the search wire shape carries no unit-bearing scalars (type/id/title/subtitle/url/score/when);
    the only display-boundary formatting is the per-row relative timestamp via DateTimeFormatting.Format(Relative).

